WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.211
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.511 --> 00:00:08.677
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:14.822
Unit twelve: Adjectives (basic). Today you will describe people and things with adjectives.

4
00:00:15.122 --> 00:00:17.995
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:22.317
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.183 --> 00:00:23.999
Big.

7
00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:26.902
Big means large in size.

8
00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:29.180
I live in a big house.

9
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:32.331
Your turn. Say: Big.

10
00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:35.866
Big.

11
00:00:36.617 --> 00:00:37.548
Small.

12
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.457
Small means little in size.

13
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.388
A mouse is small.

14
00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:45.287
Your turn. Say: Small.

15
00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.030
Small.

16
00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:50.529
Happy.

17
00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.180
Happy means feeling good.

18
00:00:53.783 --> 00:00:55.237
She is happy today.

19
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:58.061
Your turn. Say: Happy.

20
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:01.483
Happy.

21
00:01:02.217 --> 00:01:03.125
Sad.

22
00:01:04.117 --> 00:01:06.209
Sad means feeling unhappy.

23
00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:08.549
He is sad about the news.

24
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.477
Your turn. Say: Sad.

25
00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:15.230
Sad.

26
00:01:15.983 --> 00:01:16.880
Beautiful.

27
00:01:17.883 --> 00:01:20.034
Beautiful means very nice to look at.

28
00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.104
Angkor Wat is beautiful.

29
00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:25.323
Your turn. Say: Beautiful.

30
00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:29.272
Beautiful.

31
00:01:30.017 --> 00:01:30.995
Describe.

32
00:01:31.983 --> 00:01:35.074
Describe means to say what someone or something is like.

33
00:01:35.683 --> 00:01:37.021
Describe your friend.

34
00:01:37.617 --> 00:01:40.362
Your turn. Say: Describe.

35
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.259
Describe.

36
00:01:45.017 --> 00:01:45.739
Noun.

37
00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.481
Noun means a word for a person, place or thing.

38
00:01:50.083 --> 00:01:51.235
Book is a noun.

39
00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.328
Your turn. Say: Noun.

40
00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:58.121
Noun.

41
00:01:58.883 --> 00:01:59.838
Quality.

42
00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.674
Quality means a feature that describes something.

43
00:02:04.283 --> 00:02:05.935
Kindness is a good quality.

44
00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:09.121
Your turn. Say: Quality.

45
00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:12.828
Quality.

46
00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:17.168
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.017 --> 00:02:20.817
Visal, how can you describe your best friend?

48
00:02:21.917 --> 00:02:30.019
She is kind and happy. Kind and happy are adjectives. An adjective describes a noun. It tells us more about a person or thing.

49
00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.907
Where do adjectives go?

50
00:02:34.017 --> 00:02:46.787
Usually before a noun: a big house, a small cat. After be: The house is big. The cat is small. We do not add s to adjectives.

51
00:02:47.883 --> 00:02:49.500
Can we use two adjectives?

52
00:02:50.583 --> 00:03:01.394
Yes! A big, beautiful house. We put a comma between them. Not 'bigs houses'. The adjective stays the same: a big house, big houses.

53
00:03:02.533 --> 00:03:03.952
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:08.976
Grammar focus: Adjectives: before a noun or after be.

55
00:03:09.276 --> 00:03:10.439
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.348
a big house

57
00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.553
She is happy today.

58
00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:16.765
a beautiful garden

59
00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:23.374
An adjective describes a noun. Put it before the noun or after be. It never takes an s.

60
00:03:24.117 --> 00:03:27.675
Be careful! Don't say: She has a beautifuls dog.

61
00:03:29.633 --> 00:03:31.633
Say: She has a beautiful dog.

62
00:03:31.933 --> 00:03:34.037
Adjectives never take an s.

63
00:03:34.833 --> 00:03:37.637
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:38.433 --> 00:03:39.609
My Best Friend.

65
00:03:39.909 --> 00:03:41.966
My best friend is kind and happy.

66
00:03:42.967 --> 00:03:45.256
She has a small dog and a big smile.

67
00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:48.893
Her house is beautiful, and her garden is quiet.

68
00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.445
When I am sad, she is always near.

69
00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:57.081
We describe people with adjectives, and each quality is special.

70
00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:02.052
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:02.917 --> 00:04:05.430
She has a blank dog. (not big)

72
00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:09.697
A, small. B, smalls. C, smally.

73
00:04:13.233 --> 00:04:15.117
The answer is A: small.

74
00:04:16.283 --> 00:04:18.643
I am blank today because it is my birthday.

75
00:04:18.943 --> 00:04:22.097
A, sad. B, happy. C, angry.

76
00:04:25.633 --> 00:04:27.528
The answer is B: happy.

77
00:04:28.683 --> 00:04:30.253
Which sentence is correct?

78
00:04:30.553 --> 00:04:35.333
A, They are happys.. B, They are happy.. C, They happy are..

79
00:04:38.867 --> 00:04:40.913
The answer is B: They are happy..

80
00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.736
Angkor Wat is very blank.

81
00:04:44.036 --> 00:04:47.631
A, beautiful. B, beautifuls. C, beauty.

82
00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:53.271
The answer is A: beautiful.

83
00:04:54.417 --> 00:04:56.776
According to the reading, what is beautiful?

84
00:04:57.076 --> 00:05:00.683
A, her house. B, my dog. C, my school.

85
00:05:04.233 --> 00:05:06.233
The answer is A: her house.

86
00:05:07.433 --> 00:05:10.376
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:11.217 --> 00:05:14.551
Describe your best friend using three different adjectives.

88
00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:24.850
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:37.911
My best friend is kind, funny and clever. She is kind because she helps me. She is funny because she makes me laugh. She is clever because she studies hard. These adjectives describe my friend.

90
00:05:38.211 --> 00:05:39.897
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:40.783 --> 00:05:46.036
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and adjectives: before a noun or after be.

92
00:05:46.336 --> 00:05:49.859
Today's value is kindness. Be kind to everyone.

93
00:05:50.159 --> 00:05:52.928
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

94
00:05:53.228 --> 00:05:55.532
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

